o some exemplary data showing  that and we also give suggestions about  what kind of biopsy needle you should  use if you want to have really enough  cells for certain kind of downstream  applications thank you  what kind of cell viability and purities  do you usually see after tumor cell  isolation  okay so of course that depends on the on  the starting material so if you have a  very big chunk of to more usually when  you when you cut it you will see that  there's a lot of necrotic part in the  inner part so if you remove that usually  that improves the sample in the  beginning but some people are also  interested in the cells that are  residing is hypoxic Nisha's so they do  not want to remove it so I would say the  the purity is usually always above 90 95  percent even when you start with  challenging samples as you have seen for  example in a pleural effusion when you  have less than 2% tumor cells it can be  very high and the viability again it  depends on the target and on the  starting material but usually they are  above 80%  thank you and our last question is I'm  interested in mouse fibroblasts  associated to the tumor  micro-environment  what would be the best way to get them  yeah thank you very much so due to time  reasons I had no chance today to go into  that topic we have also worked this out  in the last two years and this is a very  challenging a population because it's a  very rare population so for four mice we  have just recently released a method  it's our to my associates file blast  isolation kit and it's a it's a two step  isolation so you first deplete the non  fiberglass or the tumour cells and the  other lineages and then there's the  second enrichment step where you  actively isolate the fiberglass this is  for the mouse system for the human  system we are still working on that  so for you therefore for human tumor  tissue currently I think that the best  choice would be to do depletion of cd45  maybe in addition also deplete your  tumor cells if you for example work with  carcinoma by FM depletion so depletion  of cd45 and FM and then subsequently an  enrichment of CD 90 positive cells  because that is so far the best marker  for tumor associated v loss we have  figured out because some of the other  published markets like the pdgfr i find  better they can be expressed on tumor  associated fibrous but we have seen them  frequently not being expressed so I  would say really CD 90 is the best  positive marker but please combine it  with a prior depletion step to pre  enrich it because he says are pretty  rare and many tumors  thank you I would like to once again  thank dr. Hart for his presentation  do you have any final comments for us  thank you all for attending the webinar  today and yeah hope to be back in the in  the future  we would like to thank our sponsor  Milton E biotech for underwriting  today's educational webcast this webcast  can be viewed on-demand to November 2018  lab routes will alert you via email when  it's available for replay we encourage  you to share that email with your  colleagues who may have missed today's  live events until next time goodbye
 

